Text: A verb pattern is either an idiom pattern or a conceptualized pattern. Idiom Pattern is in the form of verb $Iobject (e.g. eat $Ihumble pie). Conceptual- ized Pattern is in the form of verb $Cconcept (e.g. eat $Cmeal). We denote the concept in a conceptualized pattern a as ca. Deﬁnition 1 (Pattern Assignment). A pattern assignment is a function f : P →A that maps an arbitrary phrase p to its pattern a. f(p) = a means the pattern of p is a.

